eneralized fad diet to  people in need of unique Medical  Nutrition Therapy Pharmaceuticals and  comprehensive care but anyway this will  be a huge shocker to you probably but  this diet is riddled with inaccuracies  and contradictions honestly too many to  list but I want to focus in on his  lectin argument because I keep seeing  this pop up in my feeds so first of all  lectins are a group of proteins that can  be found in all plants but are most  abundant in raw legumes like beans  lentils peas soybeans and peanuts and  whole grains like wheat they're known as  phytohemoglutinins which are a class of  protein molecules that bind to  particular carbohydrates like glucose  sucrose and cellulose fiber the effect  that lectins can have on the human body  really does vary and depend on how the  lectin-containing food is prepared and  how much is consumed but the most  dramatic side effect that we've seen is  where people eat raw or undercooked  kidney beans in these rare cases the  lectins have caused red blood cells to  Clump together causing devastating  effects usually though eating them in  excess just causes GI distress like  bloating gas nausea and diarrhea in the  longer term eating raw High lectin Foods  may also interfere with mineral  absorption and because lectins bind to  the lining of the digestive tract they  can affect our good gut bacteria this is  really the Crux of the lectin phobia  Central to gendry's book and this is  where the concept of leaky gut has  really taken off if you haven't heard  the term being thrown around by wellness  influencers and natural health gurus  best you hear it from me first the first  thing you need to know is that leaky gut  is not a legitimate medical diagnosis  rather what they're referring to is  intestinal permeability which can be  affected by a number of factors so the  lining of your intestines are covered in  little finger-like projections known as  microvilli people disappear in the  Finger Lakes and these little fingers  help your gut to absorb important  nutrients and are really like the  gateway to your bloodstream AKA your  nutrient transportation system if the  microvilli or lining gets damaged for  any reason then unwanted substances like  bacteria can pass into your bloodstream  causing all sorts of problems like in  inflammation so we see intestinal  permeability in action in two main ways  firstly under stress conditions like  endurance exercise or pregnancy and  second in patients who suffer from  things like celiacs or Crohn's disease  the difference between the two is that  the leaky gut experienced under stress  conditions can be reversed using dietary  factors like introducing probiotics  whereas diseases like celiacs and  Crohn's it cannot but let's use celiac  disease as an example and just focus on  that because it's linked with a dietary  component of gluten which Dr gundry  loves to hate now when patients that  suffer from celiac disease eat gluten  the gluten leaks out of their gut and as  a result the body attacks it causing  inflammation and damage now obviously a  number of health influencers will  extrapolate this information to claim  that gluten will have this effect on  everyone and not just those with  Celiac's disease but what what is gluten  this is pretty sad because I don't know  and Dr gundry  tea by saying that it's not just gluten  it's all lectins in all forms  so we gotta remove them all P.S this is  just a sidebar but despite what Dr  gundry claims gluten is not even elected  like we find gluten in foods that  contain lectins like whole grain bread  but they're not the same components so  yeah just one of many confusions and  inaccuracies in this book but back to  his claims because the one that got  celebrities like Kelly Clarkson and  Usher was the promise of weight loss now  Dr gundry explains the link between  lectins and weight by suggesting that  lectins mimic insulin AKA what  influencers call the fat storage hormone  so by gundry's Logic when you eat  lectins you're increasing your body's  fat storage and ultimately your weight  where does he get the data to support  this claim well from a single study done  in 1980 on isolated fat cells from rats  in a Petri dish seems on brand but  anyway in the study high levels of  lectins reduced insulin sensitivity and  this led to higher levels of circulating  insulin which he concluded would cause  weight gain now besides the fact that  high insulin levels are not the cause of  weight gain check out my video on  insulin and weight gain right here you  can't just take animal studies like this  and apply the findings to living humans  in this study the rat's fat cells were  soaked in lectins in a Petri dish  there's no evidence that lectins  consumed in like beans can even get into  our fat cells not to mention how much  volume consumed would be needed to even  come close to the volume directly  applied to the rat's fat cell it's an  outrageous assertion based on again  nothing more than a far-fetched Theory  the more likely reason for celebrities  weight loss success on this diet is less  to do with lectin's insulin-like  properties and more to do with the fact  that you're just cutting a ton of food  out the plant Paradox diet includes a  three-day cleanse to start four to six  weeks of repair and restore and then a  maintenance phase where you reintroduce  some of the foods that you eliminated  before now the cleanse is really strict  removing all dairy grains or pseudo  grains fruit sugar seeds egg soy  Nightshade plants roots or tubers corn  soy canola or other inflammatory oils  with no mention of what these even  include along with any form of beef or  other farm animal meat basically you'll  be eating a handful of approved  vegetables small portions of wild caught  fish pasteurized chicken corn products  tempeh or hemp tofu as well as avocado  and a few approved oils now in the  repair and restore phase you can eat a  little more things but 