ke  another huge strike for the anti-electin  movement to me now before the comment  Warriors like get at me I need to share  that a lot of plant Paradox Defenders  will insist that Dr gundry doesn't  explicitly say you shouldn't eat legumes  they say you can have legumes if they're  cooked a certain way and this Nuance is  confusing because for like 90 of the  book he goes on about how dangerous  lectins are and how you need to get them  like the [ __ ] out of your life but to  not lose the vegan and vegetarian  consumers he makes the following  statement a pressure cooker will destroy  the lectins in beans and other legumes  which are a fantastic source of  non-vegetable protein as well as in  vegetables in The Nightshade and squash  families actually fruits better yet  pressure cooked beans shorn of their  offending lectins serve as a smorgasbord  for your gut buddies and can improve  longevity and enhance memory  uh what so all this time he's been going  on about how these exact foods are  basically killing us and all you needed  to do was cook them and all of a sudden  they're a smorgasbord for your gut  um  don't we all do this anyway like who was  eating raw beans who was eating dried  wheat berries as a snack it seems like  he needed a solid scary fear-mongering  hook to get people in and then needed to  like fill some pages to fulfill his book  contract but the book would have been  complete if he just wrote on page one  hey kids cook your beans I don't agree  with gundry on a lot of things but I do  agree with this we absolutely should not  be eating a lot of raw or active lectins  they can and do make people pretty sick  but the way these foods are consumed  almost exclusively drastically  inactivates the lectin levels lectins  are typically found on the outer surface  of foods and their water soluble  proteins so by soaking them or cooking  them using any kind of high heat  water-based method like boiling or  stewing you're going to inactivate about  94 